WEBVTT

00:01.490 --> 00:04.200
Seika? Seika?

00:04.200 --> 00:06.400
Where are you?

00:06.400 --> 00:08.380
Why don't we have some tea?

00:08.950 --> 00:11.320
I'd love to chat some more...

00:11.710 --> 00:12.490
Huh?

00:12.490 --> 00:15.500
Seika? Have you gone out for a walk?

00:17.080 --> 00:18.280
Seika!

00:18.760 --> 00:19.950
Seika?

00:20.320 --> 00:21.960
Seika!

00:21.960 --> 00:24.490
Where are you?!

00:26.280 --> 00:29.920
The princess seems to have 
taken quite a liking to you.

00:29.920 --> 00:31.170
Yeah, I guess.

00:31.170 --> 00:35.900
Oh, I wanted to inquire about her 
being able to see the future.

00:35.900 --> 00:41.180
Couldn't you use your fortune-telling 
magic to do the same thing?

00:41.180 --> 00:43.560
Fortune-telling and seeing the 
future are different things.

00:43.830 --> 00:46.720
A fortune-teller needs tools 
and advance information.

00:46.720 --> 00:48.970
And there's a limit to 
how much they can learn.

00:48.970 --> 00:51.230
Seeing the future is 
something totally different.

00:51.870 --> 00:56.530
Could she possibly become a threat to you?

00:56.530 --> 00:58.780
No, it'll be fine.

00:59.240 --> 01:00.630
As long as I don't get too involved...

01:00.630 --> 01:02.950
Seika!

01:21.220 --> 01:32.310
<b>The Reincarnation of
the Strongest Exorcist in Another World</b>

02:36.240 --> 02:38.080
Don't scare me like that!

02:38.080 --> 02:39.600
Sorry, sorry!

02:39.600 --> 02:41.470
Where are you going with that sword?

02:41.710 --> 02:44.590
Your brother was helping me practice.

02:45.550 --> 02:47.790
I couldn't win a single match.

02:47.790 --> 02:50.060
I should've expected your brother to be good.

02:50.060 --> 02:53.030
<i>I'd rather not have people 
know he's my brother.</i>

02:53.030 --> 02:55.360
Why do you look so upset?

02:56.120 --> 02:59.610
<i>But why can't Amyu beat Gly?</i>

02:59.980 --> 03:03.920
<i>She's got talent, and more 
than anything, she's the hero.</i>

03:03.920 --> 03:05.530
What are you up to?

03:06.210 --> 03:08.290
Hiding from the princess.

03:08.290 --> 03:12.130
Yeah, she really likes you.

03:12.130 --> 03:14.130
We're leaving tomorrow, though.

03:14.380 --> 03:17.660
Why not spend a little time 
talking to her before we go?

03:17.660 --> 03:22.580
She was up on the terrace moving chess 
pieces around by herself. She looked sad.

03:27.400 --> 03:30.140
You're not going to ask somebody to play?

03:30.450 --> 03:36.320
Nobody will play against me anymore.
They say they can't win.

03:36.320 --> 03:39.700
Seika, do you know how to play chess?

03:39.700 --> 03:41.650
I know the rules.

03:41.900 --> 03:44.180
Then, please play me!

03:44.180 --> 03:50.450
If nobody can beat you, 
a beginner like me's got no hope.

03:51.710 --> 03:54.460
Of course, I'll play with fewer pieces!

03:56.420 --> 03:58.920
Is it really a game with that few pieces?

03:59.200 --> 04:01.680
Hmm, that's a good question!

04:01.680 --> 04:04.340
Now, you make the first move, Seika.

04:04.560 --> 04:09.280
You sure? I'm not good enough to hold back.

04:09.280 --> 04:11.060
So I'll win for real.

04:11.060 --> 04:12.290
Go ahead.

04:12.290 --> 04:14.200
If you can.

04:14.200 --> 04:18.230
Oh, right! If you're that insistent, 
why don't we bet something?

04:18.230 --> 04:19.150
Bet?

04:19.150 --> 04:20.240
Yes.

04:20.240 --> 04:24.780
The loser has to do one thing the 
winner says, no matter what it is.

04:26.110 --> 04:28.410
That's pretty big...

04:28.880 --> 04:32.560
If it's something you really 
can't do, you can refuse.

04:32.560 --> 04:34.040
How about it?

04:34.540 --> 04:35.890
All right.

04:35.890 --> 04:36.940
Let's do it.

04:43.990 --> 04:49.350
Seika, what do you think the 
strongest chess piece in the world is?

04:50.250 --> 04:51.780
Hm...

04:51.780 --> 04:57.230
In this case, it would be you and me.

04:57.520 --> 05:00.630
We control not only the soldiers, 
but the king himself.

05:00.630 --> 05:06.840
Politicians who can never be killed on 
the battlefield are the strongest pieces.

05:06.840 --> 05:10.510
Oh, my! What a pleasing answer.

05:10.510 --> 05:14.750
Most people would say the king,
or the dragon knight.

05:15.040 --> 05:18.810
Yours is the answer I was looking for.

05:18.810 --> 05:20.380
Then, am I right?

05:22.080 --> 05:23.350
I'm not sure.

05:23.350 --> 05:26.300
But I can say that I feel differently.

05:26.690 --> 05:31.350
The strongest pieces are the ones right here.

05:32.010 --> 05:34.370
There's nothing here on this table.

05:34.370 --> 05:40.810
But in reality, the soldiers, kings, and
politicians are surrounded by many people.

05:40.810 --> 05:44.070
The people who live in this world.

05:44.710 --> 05:47.940
So you think the strongest 
pieces are the nameless masses?

05:47.940 --> 05:48.960
Yes.

05:48.960 --> 05:53.560
It's true that in some cases, a people's 
rebellion can overthrow the government.

05:53.560 --> 05:58.460
But in most cases, the people are powerless, 
and exist only to be exploited.

05:58.460 --> 06:01.600
Kings and politicians don't create anything.

06:01.600 --> 06:07.130
They simply steal the crops and resources 
the people produce, calling them "taxes."

06:07.440 --> 06:11.980
You're a princess, you know. 
You shouldn't be saying that.

06:13.120 --> 06:16.800
Politicians can't exist without taxes.

06:16.800 --> 06:20.870
That's why we can't destroy 
them, no matter what.

06:20.870 --> 06:21.900
And also,

06:22.600 --> 06:27.440
the people possess an overwhelming 
numerical advantage.

06:27.440 --> 06:33.460
And that's why you're going out of your way 
to make sure the people know your name?

06:33.460 --> 06:34.640
Yes.

06:34.640 --> 06:38.670
I don't have any kings or 
dragon knights on my side.

06:38.670 --> 06:41.740
So I prefer to use a piece that 
nobody's paying attention to.

06:41.740 --> 06:44.630
Especially if it's the strongest of them all.

06:44.630 --> 06:48.050
By the way, I'm going to win this.

06:48.050 --> 06:51.560
You've seen it already? 
With your future sight?

06:52.890 --> 07:00.100
<b>Episode 11:   Future Sight</b>

06:53.640 --> 06:55.460
Oh, my. Gly told you?

06:55.460 --> 06:56.420
Yes.

06:56.420 --> 07:00.100
But I'd realized something was 
up before he said anything.

07:00.540 --> 07:03.230
You knew that Gly would 
lose his fight with me.

07:03.520 --> 07:08.150
And that those boards would fall on you.

07:08.150 --> 07:12.570
So when Gly told me you could see 
the future, I finally understood.

07:13.230 --> 07:16.740
I owe Gly my thanks, then.

07:17.500 --> 07:21.920
I wasn't sure how I was going to tell you.

07:22.290 --> 07:27.310
When I learned about this power, 
I realized the reason I was born.

07:27.750 --> 07:33.140
To help the empire with your 
ability to see the future?

07:33.570 --> 07:34.610
No.

07:34.610 --> 07:37.460
Even if you can see the future, it changes.

07:37.460 --> 07:41.850
Heaven does not assign 
meaning to people's lives.

07:42.070 --> 07:47.550
When I realized that, I decided 
that instead of staying locked up,

07:47.550 --> 07:50.280
I'd decide for myself how I lived my life.

07:52.930 --> 07:56.060
Seika, you're losing quite badly.

07:56.060 --> 07:57.370
Will you continue?

07:57.370 --> 08:00.500
Of course I will. I won't 
give up until the end.

08:00.500 --> 08:01.870
How wonderful!

08:02.180 --> 08:05.750
But you're going to lose in seven moves.

08:08.160 --> 08:09.670
I surrender.

08:09.670 --> 08:11.630
You really are strong.

08:12.900 --> 08:16.220
You're not going to tell me that it's 
unfair that I can see the future?

08:16.220 --> 08:20.720
Nope. I just think you're 
strong at this game.

08:20.720 --> 08:22.960
That makes me happy.

08:22.960 --> 08:28.640
But I wanted you to say that 
I would never do something so unfair.

08:28.640 --> 08:31.280
Of course, I've got no way of knowing that.

08:31.280 --> 08:32.450
Oh, my.

08:32.450 --> 08:36.450
Then what would make you trust me?

08:36.450 --> 08:41.870
Most people would say tell me what you're
<i>really</i> thinking, or tell me a weakness you have.

08:44.080 --> 08:45.470
All right.

08:45.470 --> 08:48.040
I'll tell you a weakness, then.

08:48.950 --> 08:52.170
When I was a little, I was scared of stew.

08:52.170 --> 08:53.970
You didn't like it?

08:53.970 --> 08:55.840
No, I loved it.

08:55.840 --> 09:00.760
I was especially scared of eating it in 
winter, in rooms with a fireplace.

09:00.760 --> 09:07.080
I knew that stew and bread both 
had flour in them, and one day,

09:07.080 --> 09:09.650
I got an idea in my little head.

09:09.650 --> 09:15.490
If I ate stew and then slept 
with my belly towards the fire,

09:15.490 --> 09:19.580
wouldn't the stew turn into bread 
and swell up inside my body?

09:19.580 --> 09:21.200
Are you serious?

09:21.200 --> 09:22.800
I am.

09:22.800 --> 09:24.320
So when I was little,

09:24.320 --> 09:28.500
whenever I finished my stew, I would run to the coldest room in the house.

09:30.450 --> 09:35.880
You'd normally be punished for 
laughing at a princess, you know.

09:36.360 --> 09:40.750
I'm sorry. But anybody, no matter 
how loyal, would laugh at that.

09:40.750 --> 09:43.520
Next, I'll tell you what I'm really thinking.

09:44.150 --> 09:48.440
To use an example, I want to save someone.

09:50.120 --> 09:55.530
Let's say there's a child playing 
in a field, next to a huge hole.

09:55.760 --> 09:59.160
But the child doesn't know it's there.

09:59.160 --> 10:01.200
And soon, they'll fall into it.

10:01.200 --> 10:04.370
I want to save them.

10:04.370 --> 10:05.530
Is that...?

10:06.440 --> 10:09.520
I'm sorry. I can't say more than that.

10:09.520 --> 10:13.460
It might change the future 
in a way I can't predict.

10:13.770 --> 10:16.380
And that's why you wanted to see Amyu?

10:16.600 --> 10:17.840
Well...

10:17.840 --> 10:20.550
You're free to think that.

10:20.550 --> 10:25.430
And this is all something you've 
decided entirely on your own?

10:27.200 --> 10:29.200
I'll support you, then.

10:29.200 --> 10:32.730
If there's something I can do, just tell me.

10:33.600 --> 10:35.200
That makes me happy.

10:35.680 --> 10:38.110
I had fun, Seika.

10:38.320 --> 10:40.460
So did I.

10:41.450 --> 10:46.620
I'll think carefully about 
what to ask you to do.

10:48.400 --> 10:50.680
<i>Crap. I'd hoped she'd forgotten that.</i>

10:57.730 --> 10:59.780
Humans are the best!

10:59.780 --> 11:05.260
The only times I enjoy this 
trip are when I'm eating meat!

11:08.240 --> 11:11.860
Hey, Captain, can I take him with us?

11:11.860 --> 11:14.200
No. He'll attract too much attention.

11:14.200 --> 11:17.570
And he's not as powerful as your monsters.

11:17.570 --> 11:18.890
Okay.

11:18.890 --> 11:21.950
Meede, you can eat him, too.

11:25.120 --> 11:27.830
Is he yummy? There's plenty more!

11:28.850 --> 11:31.460
I'm so full...

11:31.460 --> 11:34.790
Um, Zor, please eat something.

11:34.790 --> 11:38.240
You've just been standing 
there this whole time.

11:38.240 --> 11:44.720
No, I'm fine. Thanks to all of you, I barely 
had to exert myself in that last fight.

11:44.980 --> 11:47.350
Just don't overdo it.

11:49.210 --> 11:51.440
<i>Muderev, the strongest ogre.</i>

11:51.990 --> 11:54.350
<i>Lo Ni. A powerful tamer.</i>

11:54.790 --> 11:56.770
<i>Pyrslaria uses the evil eye.</i>

11:56.970 --> 11:59.610
<i>And Gull Ganis, the devil.</i>

12:00.060 --> 12:02.450
<i>A candidate to become the 
next head of the Black Clan.</i>

12:02.970 --> 12:07.590
<i>They're all strong, and they've gotten 
stronger over the course of this journey.</i>

12:08.300 --> 12:11.370
Everyone, make sure to 
replenish your strength.

12:11.370 --> 12:12.580
Okay!

12:11.370 --> 12:12.580
Yes, sir!

12:11.370 --> 12:12.580
Right!

12:13.100 --> 12:15.520
<i>The power to see others' strengths.</i>

12:15.520 --> 12:17.290
<i>Once, I couldn't tell anyone about it.</i>

12:16.840 --> 12:20.920
<b>Zormnem</b>

12:17.840 --> 12:20.920
<i>I didn't understand why I had this power.</i>

12:21.180 --> 12:23.000
<i>There were times when it upset me.</i>

12:23.590 --> 12:25.370
<i>But now, it doesn't matter.</i>

12:26.280 --> 12:30.750
<i>It will help me achieve my goal.</i>

12:32.800 --> 12:34.590
You haven't forgotten anything?

12:34.590 --> 12:36.690
I'm fine, Brother Luft.

12:37.030 --> 12:39.490
Have fun at school.

12:39.490 --> 12:40.110
Yeah.

12:40.110 --> 12:44.960
And decide what you're going to do when 
you've graduated the lower grades.

12:44.960 --> 12:48.740
Father would like you to continue 
your studies, I'm sure, but...

12:50.000 --> 12:51.970
Oh, yeah. I know.

12:51.970 --> 12:55.460
<i>I'll keep quiet about wanting to be 
an adventurer until the last minute.</i>

12:56.180 --> 12:57.920
You, too, Yifa.

12:57.920 --> 13:00.880
You were working the whole time 
you were here. Did you get any rest?

13:01.880 --> 13:03.140
I'm fine.

13:03.140 --> 13:05.470
You take care of your health, too.

13:05.740 --> 13:07.350
You two take care, too.

13:07.350 --> 13:09.920
Please come by again
if you ever have a chance.

13:09.920 --> 13:12.570
Thank you.

13:12.570 --> 13:15.940
I wanted to stay here forever.

13:15.940 --> 13:17.960
You were slacking off the whole time.

13:17.960 --> 13:19.820
Are you like that at home?

13:19.820 --> 13:22.030
I pretend to be a good girl at home.

13:22.030 --> 13:23.780
So it's exhausting.

13:23.780 --> 13:25.560
Pretend to be a good girl here.

13:25.560 --> 13:29.490
Now I know why some of the girls 
say they want to marry a noble.

13:29.490 --> 13:34.050
Even if you do marry a noble, that doesn't 
mean you get to slack off all day.

13:34.050 --> 13:36.080
Why would you say something so mean?

13:36.080 --> 13:39.810
Once we get back to school, 
let's both study hard.

13:40.390 --> 13:41.960
I don't wanna...

13:41.960 --> 13:44.520
Seika! It's time to go!

13:44.520 --> 13:45.800
Hurry it up.

13:45.800 --> 13:49.550
Sorry, Gly. I was keeping them.

13:50.550 --> 13:51.440
Oh, fine, then.

13:51.440 --> 13:52.180
Bye.

13:52.180 --> 13:53.430
Take care, brother.

13:53.430 --> 13:54.390
Gly.

13:54.860 --> 13:56.210
What?

13:56.210 --> 13:58.650
You're coming to the capital 
once in a while right?

13:58.650 --> 14:01.520
We can see each other then.

14:01.520 --> 14:03.740
Yes, that's right.

14:03.740 --> 14:09.360
Assuming Gly doesn't die battling an
assassin who's been sent to get me.

14:09.650 --> 14:11.850
Don't say that! It'll come true!

14:11.850 --> 14:13.190
It's just a joke.

14:13.190 --> 14:15.980
And I'm the one saying it's a joke.

14:15.980 --> 14:17.410
So don't worry about it.

14:17.410 --> 14:18.710
R-Right.

14:19.150 --> 14:24.860
Lord Luft, I apologize for the trouble 
I caused during my long stay.

14:24.860 --> 14:27.000
Not at all, Princess.

14:27.000 --> 14:28.720
I will continue to govern my lands

14:28.720 --> 14:32.450
and advance the study of magic, 
so that the empire may prosper.

14:33.090 --> 14:34.860
Bye, Brother Luft.

14:34.860 --> 14:35.770
Take care.

14:35.770 --> 14:37.600
You, too, Seika.

14:37.600 --> 14:38.480
Bye.

14:47.780 --> 14:51.360
You really do stop talking the 
minute you get in a carriage.

14:51.360 --> 14:54.120
I don't want to do anything 
that'll make me sicker.

14:54.770 --> 14:57.790
This carriage shakes less than most...

14:58.230 --> 15:01.450
I'm sorry I can't give 
you someone to talk to.

15:01.450 --> 15:02.670
It's fine.

15:02.670 --> 15:06.770
I didn't think there was anything in the 
world that could make you feel sick.

15:06.770 --> 15:08.590
I am human, you know.

15:09.950 --> 15:11.260
I don't know about that.

15:15.430 --> 15:18.960
Hey, is it safe for you 
to be here, Brother Gly?

15:18.960 --> 15:20.730
You're the captain of the soldiers, right?

15:20.730 --> 15:22.210
It's fine.

15:22.210 --> 15:25.440
My top priority is staying by the 
princess's side to protect her.

15:25.440 --> 15:28.460
But what if something happens?

15:28.460 --> 15:33.200
We're traveling in huge numbers 
so that nothing happens.

15:33.560 --> 15:38.080
If anything <i>does</i> happen, I'll command 
the troops while protecting the princess.

15:38.080 --> 15:39.920
I'm more than capable of that.

15:39.920 --> 15:41.080
Good.

15:41.300 --> 15:46.840
On a different subject, how large are 
this country's bandit groups typically?

15:46.840 --> 15:47.960
Bandits?

15:47.960 --> 15:51.840
Well, anywhere from a few 
people to a few hundred.

15:51.840 --> 15:53.060
I see.

15:53.060 --> 15:54.720
Then, what's that?

15:56.550 --> 15:57.420
What?

15:58.260 --> 16:01.740
Looks like they took out the empty 
carriage we used as a decoy.

16:02.390 --> 16:05.810
I guess something did happen.

16:08.670 --> 16:10.990
I haven't done acrobatics 
like that in a long time.

16:10.990 --> 16:13.860
B-Bandits!

16:18.410 --> 16:19.840
We got the wrong one.

16:19.840 --> 16:21.500
Topaz, go after six!

16:22.660 --> 16:24.330
Corundum, hit carriage eight!

16:24.670 --> 16:26.920
Everyone else, aim for the 
one on the carriage roof!

16:29.170 --> 16:30.510
Bows?

16:30.510 --> 16:32.050
This'll do, then.

16:33.720 --> 16:36.680
Phase of sunlight. Spell of Magnetic Storm.

16:38.350 --> 16:39.430
Fire!

16:45.440 --> 16:47.150
Looks like you need to learn to aim!

16:47.790 --> 16:49.020
Boss...

16:48.300 --> 16:50.400
Nephrite, support the attack on eight!

16:50.400 --> 16:53.500
Corundum reserve units, 
kill the one on the roof.

16:56.240 --> 16:58.820
What is that? Is it magic?

16:58.820 --> 17:01.590
Boss, six and seven were decoys too!

17:01.590 --> 17:03.880
The enemy has started their counterattack!

17:03.880 --> 17:04.810
Give us your orders!

17:05.290 --> 17:07.170
The carriage with the mage!

17:07.420 --> 17:09.500
Topaz unit, hit him with your magic!

17:12.050 --> 17:13.510
Yellow rises indomitably!

17:13.880 --> 17:19.050
Unmoving spirits of rock, let your wrath 
become a hammer and fall down upon my foes!

17:19.050 --> 17:21.140
Rock Fall!

17:23.880 --> 17:26.060
Mages are nice and easy to deal with.

17:26.320 --> 17:27.620
A barrier?

17:27.620 --> 17:29.520
Draw your swords!

17:29.520 --> 17:31.440
Forget the mage!

17:31.440 --> 17:33.990
Charge the carriage and get the target!

17:36.070 --> 17:37.880
You're all out of arrows, huh?

17:37.880 --> 17:38.450
Sheesh.

17:38.730 --> 17:40.780
Now I can finally have some fun.

17:41.150 --> 17:45.080
Everyone, this is your chance 
to save the Holy Princess!

17:45.080 --> 17:48.250
Who wants to have the 
bards sing of their valor?

17:55.590 --> 17:57.570
<i>So he can act like an officer if he wants to.</i>

17:57.570 --> 18:01.300
Seika, can you take the enemy alive?

18:02.080 --> 18:03.600
As you wish.

18:03.600 --> 18:04.590
Phase of wood.

18:04.590 --> 18:06.050
Spell of Binding Vines.

18:08.230 --> 18:09.620
What is this?

18:14.480 --> 18:15.400
How's that?

18:15.870 --> 18:17.840
I got them all.

18:19.760 --> 18:21.030
Bandits?

18:21.030 --> 18:23.210
I wondered what all that noise was.

18:23.210 --> 18:25.740
You caught them all?

18:25.740 --> 18:29.460
Yeah. Wait, you didn't notice at all?

18:30.010 --> 18:35.130
We noticed the carriage behind us wasn't 
keeping up, and quickly turned around...

18:35.130 --> 18:37.760
But by the time we got here, it was over.

18:38.330 --> 18:40.680
Looks like nobody was badly hurt.

18:40.680 --> 18:44.220
That was close. I'm glad 
we weren't caught up in it.

18:44.220 --> 18:48.000
What? If we'd been here,
 we could've beaten them all.

18:48.000 --> 18:49.550
Right, Mabel?

18:49.550 --> 18:51.810
I don't want to do anything 
that involves work.

18:51.810 --> 18:53.980
You guys sure are relaxed...

18:53.980 --> 18:58.820
It's strange they'd attack a carriage 
with an army escort, though...

18:59.150 --> 19:01.490
Yeah, it is.

19:01.490 --> 19:04.320
What are they going to do with them all?

19:04.320 --> 19:06.830
Make them all walk to the capital?

19:06.830 --> 19:09.460
No, they wouldn't go that far.

19:10.720 --> 19:12.210
Hey! Seika!

19:12.520 --> 19:14.130
The princess is calling.

19:16.410 --> 19:20.780
Thank you for capturing those assassins.

19:20.780 --> 19:22.390
So they were assassins.

19:22.390 --> 19:26.560
You took them alive to serve as evidence 
against your political enemies?

19:26.560 --> 19:33.100
Yes. Of course, I'd have to 
find out who sent them first.

19:33.370 --> 19:34.900
Any ideas?

19:34.900 --> 19:37.850
There are so many people it 
could be that I'm not sure.

19:38.780 --> 19:42.410
Are you planning on taking 
them all to the capital?

19:42.410 --> 19:44.780
Yes. Of course.

19:45.050 --> 19:48.120
You saw this would happen.

19:48.120 --> 19:50.470
Hence the extra carriages.

19:51.160 --> 19:55.700
If we had to make them all walk, 
it would delay our arrival.

19:55.700 --> 20:01.170
And it wouldn't be fair to make you 
miss the start of next semester.

20:01.170 --> 20:07.600
I appreciate that, but it's a 
mistake to try and bring them all.

20:07.600 --> 20:09.520
Oh? Why?

20:09.780 --> 20:14.400
What if they find some way to slip out 
of their bonds and attack us again?

20:14.400 --> 20:17.400
Of course, we could cut 
their Achilles heels...

20:17.400 --> 20:19.620
There's no need for that.

20:19.620 --> 20:21.890
They won't try anything.

20:21.890 --> 20:24.570
It's safer for them to 
wait for the next attack.

20:24.570 --> 20:27.280
You mean there's another group out there?

20:27.280 --> 20:29.410
Doesn't that make it even more dangerous?

20:29.410 --> 20:30.750
No.

20:30.750 --> 20:32.830
There's no need to worry about that.

20:32.830 --> 20:35.510
What they're waiting for won't come.

20:35.510 --> 20:37.750
There will be no other attack.

20:38.060 --> 20:42.020
The winds of fate blow like a gale, 
and the flapping of a butterfly's wings

20:42.020 --> 20:44.550
can do nothing to change their course.

20:45.070 --> 20:49.130
This is their destiny... 
that future will never come.

20:55.310 --> 20:57.270
It's truly a shame.

20:57.270 --> 21:01.360
I was hoping I could bring you to the court.

21:01.360 --> 21:03.120
I was hoping I could see it...

21:03.120 --> 21:05.240
I would've been able to 
brag about it forever.

21:05.240 --> 21:07.360
Aww, Amyu...

21:07.360 --> 21:10.480
She got us an expensive inn, so I'm happy.

21:10.480 --> 21:12.120
Mabel, you, too?

21:13.160 --> 21:17.790
I don't get many chances 
to talk to people my age.

21:17.790 --> 21:19.520
It was fun.

21:21.550 --> 21:23.050
I mean it.

21:24.020 --> 21:28.540
I'm sure I'll have a chance to invite you.

21:28.540 --> 21:30.430
Yes, anytime.

21:31.970 --> 21:35.070
Princess! Time to head inside!

21:35.070 --> 21:37.710
Okay, I have to go.

21:39.830 --> 21:41.690
Bye, Seika.

21:42.260 --> 21:42.860
Yeah.

21:43.380 --> 21:45.360
Take care, Brother Gly.

21:45.970 --> 21:50.450
You, too, Princess. It was an 
honor to escort you this far.

21:50.450 --> 21:52.560
Oh, my. Escort me?

21:52.560 --> 21:56.260
I thought we'd become 
friends, but I guess not...

21:56.260 --> 21:58.540
Sure, that's fine.

21:59.480 --> 22:00.710
Seika...

22:01.350 --> 22:04.220
I'm on your side.

22:07.280 --> 22:10.840
No matter what happens, 
please don't forget that.

22:23.670 --> 22:25.320
<i>Our destination is close.</i>

22:26.190 --> 22:28.410
<i>As is the end of our journey.</i>

22:29.810 --> 22:31.510
<i>It was a harsh journey.</i>

22:32.150 --> 22:37.160
<i>We were lucky to make it this far 
without losing a single person.</i>

22:37.640 --> 22:42.320
<i>When we arrive, we will have 
to do what we came here for.</i>

22:43.280 --> 22:48.590
<i>Everyone is surely aware that greater danger 
lies ahead than we have ever faced before.</i>

22:48.590 --> 22:52.020
<i>Once we defeat the hero, 
they won't let us escape alive.</i>

22:52.570 --> 22:55.060
<i>This has always been a one-way journey.</i>

22:55.550 --> 22:56.500
<i>But...</i>

22:57.390 --> 22:58.600
Listen, everyone!

22:58.600 --> 23:01.560
We will defeat the hero, 
for the sake of all demons!

23:02.000 --> 23:06.690
And when we've done that, 
we'll all head home together!

23:08.110 --> 23:12.030
What are you talking about?
That's always been the plan.

23:13.180 --> 23:15.660
I want to get in my futon 
and sleep a long time...

23:15.660 --> 23:18.950
I want to bring back some crop seeds!

23:18.950 --> 23:21.580
I want to feed them to 
the rest of my village!

23:21.580 --> 23:25.200
I want to tell everyone of my great deeds!

23:25.200 --> 23:28.210
To tell them I've avenged my brother!

23:30.050 --> 23:33.340
We shall all achieve this 
great deed together!

23:35.430 --> 23:39.100
For our future, and the future of the demons!
